      "extract": "\\label{section: Introduction} Ordinary gauge theory describes how 0-dimensional particles transform as we move them along 1-dimensional paths. It is natural to assign a group element to each path: \\[ \\xymatrix{ \\bullet \\ar@/^1pc/[rr]^{g} && \\bullet } \\] The reason is that composition of paths then corresponds to multiplication in the group: \\[ \\xymatrix{ \\bullet \\ar@/^1pc/[rr]^{g} && \\bullet \\ar@/^1pc/[rr]^{g'} &&",
